      "A 265 lb limit; heavier users should look at FOUSAE or WELLFIT",
      "A 15-inch belt, narrower than the 16-inch belts on two other picks",
      "The listing does not say what buttons, if any, are on the pad itself",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest sensible way to get a remote with an app as backup, from a brand with a long walking pad range. Best for users under about 215 lb.",
    description: "UREVO is one of the best-known walking pad brands on Amazon, and this is its entry pad. The listing gives a 15 by 39.8-inch non-slip belt, a 2.5 HP motor, a 0.6 to 4 mph speed range, a 265 lb maximum user weight and a 4.1-inch slim profile with built-in wheels. For this page, the important line is the last bullet: you start and run it with the LED display, the included remote or app control. The app connects by Bluetooth and, per the listing, tracks steps, distance, calories and time, with goals, more than 50 virtual routes, races against virtual opponents and a MIIT interval mode. That makes the app a real backup if the remote goes missing, not just a step counter. Cushioning is a five-layer belt with eight silicone shock absorbers and two rubber pads. With a sensible margin below its 265 lb limit, it suits users up to about 215 lb, and the 4 mph ceiling makes it a walking machine rather than a jogging one. Our UREVO brand page covers its bigger incline pads if you want hills. Amazon showed it at $132.99 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "walkingpad-c2",
    name: "WalkingPad C2",
    brand: "WalkingPad",
    category: "Best folding walking pad with a remote",
    badge: "Best Fold-in-Half",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F48MZV54?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31WUvcjXp-L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $363 (Amazon, 24 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":363,"high":363},
    specs: "2.0 HP · 1–4 mph · 220 lb max user · folds 180° to 5.4 in. high · 55 lb · remote and app control · FootSense (title)",
    pros: [
      "Folds in half, 180 degrees, to 5.4 inches high, per the listing",
      "Speed set by remote or app, so the app is a ready backup",
      "Smart FootSense control named in the listing title",
      "No assembly; 55 lb with two wheels for moving it",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 220 lb limit, the lowest on this page",
      "About $363, the most expensive pad here",
      "The listing does not give the belt size",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a small home where the pad must fold away under a bed or sofa, and for users comfortably under 220 lb.",
    description: "The C2 is from WalkingPad, the KingSmith brand that popularised the fold-in-half walking pad, and folding is its main reason to exist. The listing describes a deck that folds 180 degrees to a height of 5.4 inches, so the pad takes half the floor area of a flat pad when stored. It gives a 2.0 HP motor, speeds of 1 to 4 mph that can be adjusted using either the remote control or the app, a 220 lb maximum user weight, a 55 lb machine weight with two wheels, no assembly, and an LED display showing steps, time, speed, calories and distance. The title adds Smart FootSense control, which the bullets do not explain; on WalkingPad pads this is generally an automatic speed mode, so read the manual before relying on it. The listing does not state the belt size, which is why it is not in the specification line. The C2 is the most expensive pad on this page and has the lowest weight limit, so it makes sense only if the fold matters to you. Our reviews of the WalkingPad Z1 and A1 Pro cover the brand’s other folding pads. Amazon showed it at $362.57 on 24 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "goplus-walking-pad-2-5hp",
    name: "Goplus Walking Pad 2.5 HP Under Desk Treadmill",
    brand: "Goplus",
    category: "Best walking pad with a remote and no app",
    badge: "Simplest",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FHKMSTKL?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41PuPFQGuLL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $150 (Amazon, 24 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":150,"high":150},
